(5095426, 741528, 32767, '<td valign="top">Technically perfect whatever that means) but I''m not getting any energy from the guy.</td>', 'Technically perfect whatever that means) but I''m not getting any energy from the guy.', '2008-12-01 18:21:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5095487, 743027, 43774, '<td valign="top">In the morning hour<br/>She waits<br/>For a heartbeat<br/>A sigh<br/>A whisper<br/>And she remembers<br/> <br/>I''m not trying to be another <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a> with my "poem" comment, but some photos just move me. I write little poems off and on and after seeing this photo and thinking about it for a while, the poem came to me. I love the whiteness of the image (high-key, over exposure, whatever you want to call it). I love her pose and her gaze. She has a lot on her mind, we can''t tell if it is happy or sad memories, probably a little of both. It might have been a tad bit better if she were nude and you could not see the bit of clothing, but because it''s white it doesn''t make that much of a difference. This looks like <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=55838" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">aimeethetoo</a> so whoever took this photo, Tim or Aimee, you''ve done a wonderful job and it''s very deserving of a 10. I don''t normally "go crazy" for people photos, it takes a special one to move me.</td>', 'In the morning hourShe waitsFor a heartbeatA sighA whisperAnd she remembers I''m not trying to be another  K10DGuy with my "poem" comment, but some photos just move me. I write little poems off and on and after seeing this photo and thinking about it for a while, the poem came to me. I love the whiteness of the image (high-key, over exposure, whatever you want to call it). I love her pose and her gaze. She has a lot on her mind, we can''t tell if it is happy or sad memories, probably a little of both. It might have been a tad bit better if she were nude and you could not see the bit of clothing, but because it''s white it doesn''t make that much of a difference. This looks like  aimeethetoo so whoever took this photo, Tim or Aimee, you''ve done a wonderful job and it''s very deserving of a 10. I don''t normally "go crazy" for people photos, it takes a special one to move me.', '2008-12-01 18:43:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5095502, 743617, 27133, '<td valign="top">Outstanding...definitely the winner.  I predict an 8.3 score.  No vote! ;)</td>', 'Outstanding...definitely the winner.  I predict an 8.3 score.  No vote! ;)', '2008-12-01 18:51:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5095509, 743617, 82707, '<td valign="top">Awsome image! Perhaps a follow on image from ''The Last Supper''? ....10 and it gets my Blue Ribbon vote.  Good luck!</td>', 'Awsome image! Perhaps a follow on image from ''The Last Supper''? ....10 and it gets my Blue Ribbon vote.  Good luck!', '2008-12-01 18:54:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5095510, 743675, 32767, '<td valign="top">The near day-glo saturation levels (in the greens, for sure) trump most of the other things in the image. For that the image doesn''t float me even though I know someone said the regular camera/pp levels don''t do the actual colors justice. Still seems over the top. Good Luck.</td>', 'The near day-glo saturation levels (in the greens, for sure) trump most of the other things in the image. For that the image doesn''t float me even though I know someone said the regular camera/pp levels don''t do the actual colors justice. Still seems over the top. Good Luck.', '2008-12-01 18:55:19.000000', NULL, 1),
