(5108962, 743270, 76430, '<td valign="top">It''s not a particularly interesting photo, probably an outtake from "Benches", but what is interesting is that if those are stars (it''s not snow because there is none below the horizon) it must be a long exposure at night with a very dark sky and a very patient model.  I''m very interested to see how this was done.</td>', 'It''s not a particularly interesting photo, probably an outtake from "Benches", but what is interesting is that if those are stars (it''s not snow because there is none below the horizon) it must be a long exposure at night with a very dark sky and a very patient model.  I''m very interested to see how this was done.', '2008-12-05 10:11:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5108990, 740041, 76430, '<td valign="top">I like the composition a lot with the left edge alignment, figures in it, vanishing point, and finishing.  However my attention is split between the girl holding out the ice cream and the couple hugging, since they are both in the DOF, but there is no connection between them.  If the man was looking towards the little girl it would have been perfect, but obviously that was beyond your controland I suppose would have lost the face of the man also.  Otherwise if the DOF was only on the girl it would be great.  Without having actual models posing I know this is a split second decision and you did very good on it.</td>', 'I like the composition a lot with the left edge alignment, figures in it, vanishing point, and finishing.  However my attention is split between the girl holding out the ice cream and the couple hugging, since they are both in the DOF, but there is no connection between them.  If the man was looking towards the little girl it would have been perfect, but obviously that was beyond your controland I suppose would have lost the face of the man also.  Otherwise if the DOF was only on the girl it would be great.  Without having actual models posing I know this is a split second decision and you did very good on it.', '2008-12-05 10:22:13.000000', NULL, 1),
