(5109890, 737191, 18655, '<td valign="top">What a great shot! I love this - not just as a family type picture but it just tells me so much. A perfect 10 from me! Excellent!!</td>', 'What a great shot! I love this - not just as a family type picture but it just tells me so much. A perfect 10 from me! Excellent!!', '2008-12-05 15:26:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5109902, 735858, 67841, '<td valign="top">I contemplated submitting a shot against the grain, too.  We both know it can''t possibly end well, though... <br/> <br/>Regardless, your bold endeavor demands I pay closer attention!  <br/> <br/>Fairly nice bokeh from what I can tell here at this aperture.  The COC are nice &amp; not too busy, so that is pleasing.  I love the hint of a scene with the person next to the tree. She (I say ''she'' because of the colors, but I s''pose it could be a ''he'') looks like she has a picnic blanket in front of her, likely folding it up given the title.  Strong vertical elements that the grove of trees supply here adds a nice fairy tale element to the composition.  The downfall here, IMO, is the lack in contrast &amp; saturation.  I''m begging for those highlights to be contrasted by deep dark greens everywhere, not just one small tease of a patch across the centre.  <br/> <br/>This has a nice impressionistic element going strongly for it, and I like the storytelling that takes palce in the title and the action.  Ultimately a little more strength in the palette would have brought it up a notch or two for me - good luck!    -- 7 --</td>', 'I contemplated submitting a shot against the grain, too.  We both know it can''t possibly end well, though...  Regardless, your bold endeavor demands I pay closer attention!   Fairly nice bokeh from what I can tell here at this aperture.  The COC are nice & not too busy, so that is pleasing.  I love the hint of a scene with the person next to the tree. She (I say ''she'' because of the colors, but I s''pose it could be a ''he'') looks like she has a picnic blanket in front of her, likely folding it up given the title.  Strong vertical elements that the grove of trees supply here adds a nice fairy tale element to the composition.  The downfall here, IMO, is the lack in contrast & saturation.  I''m begging for those highlights to be contrasted by deep dark greens everywhere, not just one small tease of a patch across the centre.   This has a nice impressionistic element going strongly for it, and I like the storytelling that takes palce in the title and the action.  Ultimately a little more strength in the palette would have brought it up a notch or two for me - good luck!    -- 7 --', '2008-12-05 15:30:39.000000', NULL, 1),
